  },
  {
    "text": "Stakeholder RoadmapsStakeholder roadmaps are strategic views of a team or organization's in-progress work to further product objectives, tailored to your stakeholders' interests.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/stakeholder-roadmaps"
  },
  {
    "text": "StandupWhat is a standup? Standups are a key part of the agile development process. Learn more about standups and other agile practices in our resources library.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/standup"
  },
  {
    "text": "Story MappingStory mapping aligns everyone around an objective and creates a context-rich environment so it's easy to allocate resources. Read our guide.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/story-mapping"
  },
  {
    "text": "Story PointWhat is a story point? Learn the definition and the importance of standardization across development teams.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/story-point"
  },
  {
    "text": "Story PointsLearn how story points can help teams create a shared understanding about the overall effort each task will take.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/story-points"
  },
  {
    "text": "Strategic Portfolio ViewsLearn about Strategic Portfolio Views for presenting a clear picture of objectives, roadmaps, initiatives, and progress",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/strategic-portfolio-views"
  },
  {
    "text": "Sunk CostSunk cost refers to an investment that already has incurred, but can't be recovered. Sunk costs should not dictate future decisions.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/sunk-cost"
  },
  {
    "text": "SWOT AnalysisDiscover the 5-step process to conducting a SWOT analysis that will identify a strategic endeavor\u2019s strengths, weaknesses, opportunities, and threats.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/swot-analysis"
  },
  {
    "text": "Technical DebtTechnical debt is a term routinely used in the software industry by developers, product managers, and executives alike. But what is technical debt?",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/technical-debt"
  },
  {
    "text": "Technical Product ManagerWhat is a Technical Product Manager? Learn more about Technical Product Managers and other product management roles in our resources library.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/technical-product-manager"
  },
  {
    "text": "The 4 Ds of Time ManagementThe 4 Ds of time management, sometimes referred to as the 4 Ds of productivity, is a popular strategy for discerning whether or not a task or project is worth your time. It involves making a quick decision about what to act on now either by doing it yourself or delegating to someone else, what to act on in the future, or what to drop from your to-do list.The 4 Ds are: Do, Defer (Delay), Delegate, and Delete (Drop). Placing a task or project into one of these categories helps you manage your limited time more effectively and stay focused on what matters most to you.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/4-ds-of-time-management"
  },
  {
    "text": "ThemeIn product management, a theme is a high-level goal. Here's the 3 steps involved in developing your own plus their fit in product roadmaps.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/theme"
  },
  {
    "text": "The User Is Drunk\u201cThe User is Drunk\u201d is a design concept for products or websites so intuitive that someone under the influence of alcohol could use them.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/the-user-is-drunk"
  },
  {
    "text": "Timeline RoadmapA timeline roadmap serves several strategic purposes. Primarily, it communicates the priority order of a team\u2019s initiatives.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/timeline-roadmap"
  },
  {
    "text": "Top-Down Product StrategyWhat is a Top-Down Product Strategy? Learn more about Top-Down Product Strategy and other product management terms in our resources library.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/top-down-product-strategy"
  },
  {
    "text": "Total Addressable Market (TAM)What is Total Addressable Market (TAM) and how can you calculate it? Learn how TAM is used, how to understand your product or service's TAM, and more.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/total-addressable-market"
  },
  {
    "text": "Tribe Model ManagementTribe model management is part of an agile scaling strategy first used at Spotify. Discover the benefits and learn how to apply this concept to your team.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/tribe-model-management"
  },
  {
    "text": "Turnover RateFor a SaaS company, the turnover rate will include both customers who actively cancel their subscriptions and simply don\u2019t renew them.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/turnover-rate"
  },
  {
    "text": "Unique Selling PropositionA unique selling proposition is a clear and succinct description of how your product is both different from and better than your competitors.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/unique-selling-proposition"
  },
  {
    "text": "Usability TestingUsability testing refers to a technique to evaluate the difficulting of finding a company's product. Learn the 7 steps of usability testing.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/usability-testing"
  },
  {
    "text": "Use CaseWhat is a Use Case in product management? Learn more about use cases and other product management terminology in our resources library.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/use-case"
  },
  {
    "text": "User ExperienceWhat is User Experience (UX)? Learn more about UX principles, how UX and UI differ, and the value of UX design for product managers.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/user-experience"
  },
  {
    "text": "User FlowA user flow is a chart showing the path a user will take in an application to complete a task. Learn their importance and when to use them.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/user-flow"
  },
  {
    "text": "User InterfaceWhat is a User Interface (UI)? Learn more about User Interfaces and other product management terminology in our resources library.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/user-interface"
  },
  {
    "text": "User PersonaWhat are User Personas in product management? Learn more about user personas and other product management terms in our resources library.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/user-persona"
  },
  {
    "text": "User ResearchWhat is User Research? Read further for a general overview of user research along with a few commonly used research methods.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/user-research"
  },
  {
    "text": "User StoryWhat is a user story and who is responsible for them? Learn how to write user stories\u2014plus get a free user story template.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/user-story"
  },
